-- title:
--   Igusa radicand at a supersingular place: exponent coprime to p-1
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $\kappa$ a perfect field of characteristic $p$, let $M\ge 5$ be a non-zero natural number with $p\nmid M$, and let $K_0=$ [`ModularCurve.x1FunctionFieldC`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L134) $\kappa\,M$ be the intermediate field of the Laurent series field $\kappa((q))$ over $\kappa$ generated by the ratios of integral $q$-expansions of forms on $\Gamma_1(M)$. Let $w$ consist of a weight-one modular form on $\Gamma_1(M)$ together with an integral power series whose image in $\mathbb{C}[[q]]$ is the form's $q$-expansion and whose image in $\kappa((q))$ is non-zero, and write $a=w.\mathrm{hasseRootFn}$ for the inverse in $\kappa((q))$ of that image. Let $\bar\jmath\in K_0$ be the element whose Laurent series is [`ModularCurve.jqModC`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L15) $\kappa$, namely $q^{-1}$ times the reduction to $\kappa$ of the integral power series $E_4^3\cdot\eta^{-24}$-numerator of $j$. Let $O\subseteq K_0$ be a valuation subring containing the image of $\kappa$, with $O\neq K_0$ and $\bar\jmath\in O$, and assume that for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $p$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi\colon O\to\Omega$ whose kernel is the maximal ideal of $O$, the value $\varphi(\bar\jmath)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7) $p\,\Omega$, i.e. every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\Omega$ with that $j$-invariant has no non-zero affine point killed by $p$. Then there exist $b\in K_0$, an element $\varpi\in O$, a unit $u\in O^\times$ and an integer $m$ such that the Laurent series of $b$ equals $a^{p-1}$, $\varpi$ is irreducible in $O$, $m$ and $p-1$ are coprime in $\mathbb{Z}$, and $b=u\,\varpi^{m}$ in $K_0$ (integer power of $\varpi$ taken in the field).
--
--   This is the radicand condition of Kummer theory at a supersingular place: together with the description of the Igusa function field as $K_0(a)$ with $a^{p-1}=b$, it forces the Igusa covering of $X_1(M)$ to be totally ramified over supersingular points, in the form going back to Igusa and treated in Katz–Mazur. It is used in [`ModularCurve.forall_valuationSubring_igusaFunctionFieldX1C_comap_eq_imp_eq_and_exists_of_mem_ssJSet`](thm.html#ModularCurve.forall_valuationSubring_igusaFunctionFieldX1C_comap_eq_imp_eq_and_exists_of_mem_ssJSet), where the places of the Igusa field above a supersingular place are analysed.
-- source:
